# Model assets must be byte-identical on every platform.
#
# The LightGBM boosters are .txt, so git's autocrlf would check them out with CRLF on
# Windows and LF on Linux. The hosted site runs on Linux and the models are trained on
# Windows, and a forecast must not depend on which one wrote the file - so line-ending
# translation is switched off for them rather than trusting every parser in the chain
# to normalise.
app/assets/models/*.txt -text
app/assets/models/*.json -text

# Binary assets: never diffed, never translated.
*.gpkg binary
*.parquet binary
*.npz binary
*.nc binary
*.grd binary
